# text = These little ones are always right George if I thought you cross enough to think of anything that a shrill old soldier's wife -- who could have bitten her tongue off afterwards and ought to have done it almost -- said this morning , I don't know what I shouldn't say to you now My kind soul of a darling Not a morsel of it Because really and truly , George , what I said and meant to say was that I trusted Lignum to you and was sure you'd bring him through it .
